				"o-msdsz1ty-d72d7110"
			],
			"doesNotFund": "A lowered text_like constant. The pre-registered gates all PASS on the section-B sample, but that sample is truncated at the cut by construction and holds exactly one negative answer, so its \"optimum\" of 0.301998 at J 1.000 measures where the sample was cut, not where the boundary is. Pooling round 1's 31 unconditioned text_like rows back in restores the keep side and the J gain falls to 0.0000 — the J-gain gate FAILS. Moving the global cut down to 0.514847 would buy recall (24.4% -> 46.7%) at a precision cost (100.0% -> 91.3%) for no J gain at all.",
			"recommends": "A per-cover rescue rule rather than a lower global cut — on a cover where NO text_like mask clears the cut, admit that cover's strongest text_like mask down to a floor — fitted on a round that samples both sides of the boundary on hard covers. Not fundable from this round."
